<div class="modal-content">
  <div class="modal-header">
    <button class="modal-close" @click="$refs.helpDialog.close()" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h2 id="help-modal-title">Quick Reference</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="modal-body">

  <p>Please see our
    <a href="https://kanjialive.com/user-guide/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="User Guide (opens in new tab)">User Guide</a> for detailed explanations of all of <em>Kanji alive's</em> features or watch our
    <a href="https://www.youtube.com/kanjialive/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="short demonstration videos (opens in new tab)">short demonstration videos</a>. If you are having technical difficulties, please refer to our
    <a href="https://kanjialive.com/troubleshooting/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Troubleshooting (opens in new tab)">Troubleshooting</a> page.
  </p>
  <p lang="ja">詳細は、メニューの「日本語」内にある使用説明とトラブルシューティングをご参照ください。</p>

  <%# Arrow glyphs are aria-hidden with a visually-hidden name beside them: screen
      readers skip ←→↑↓ at default punctuation verbosity, leaving "Use the and keys". %>
  <h3>Navigation</h3>
  <table class="help-table">
    <caption class="visually-hidden">Detail view navigation: action, and how to do it</caption>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Next/Previous kanji</th>
      <td>Use the <kbd aria-hidden="true">&larr;</kbd><span class="visually-hidden">Left arrow</span> and <kbd aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</kbd><span class="visually-hidden">Right arrow</span> keys or click on the left and right single pointed brackets in the top navigation bar</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Toggle kanji animation/typeface</th>
      <td>Use the <kbd aria-hidden="true">&uarr;</kbd><span class="visually-hidden">Up arrow</span> or <kbd aria-hidden="true">&darr;</kbd><span class="visually-hidden">Down arrow</span> keys or click on the large image of the kanji.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Next/Previous typeface</th>
      <td>Use the <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd aria-hidden="true">&larr;</kbd><span class="visually-hidden">Left arrow</span> and <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</kbd><span class="visually-hidden">Right arrow</span> keys or click on the left and right single pointed brackets next to the name of the typeface</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Return to Search</th>
      <td>Click on the text of the current search term on the far left of the navigation bar</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
  <p>
    Note: The order in which kanji appear in the detail view when selecting the next or previous kanji is dependant on the sort mode previously chosen in the search view.
  </p>

  <h3>Other Interactive Elements</h3>
  <table class="help-table">
    <caption class="visually-hidden">Interactive elements: element, and how to use it</caption>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Play/Pause kanji animation</th>
      <td>Use the <kbd>spacebar</kbd> or click on the play/pause icon in the center of the kanji animation controls.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Next/Previous stroke</th>
      <td>Use the <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd aria-hidden="true">&larr;</kbd><span class="visually-hidden">Left arrow</span> or <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</kbd><span class="visually-hidden">Right arrow</span> keys, click the previous and next stroke icons on each side of the play/pause icon or move your mouse cursor over the stroke breakdown images.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Radical animation</th>
      <td>Use the <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>r</kbd> keys or click on the image on the far right of the radical field to view an animation illustrating the radical's historical derivation.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Examples</th>
      <td>Move your mouse cursor over a Japanese word in the Examples field to reveal its English meaning. Click on the play icon to the right of each example to hear its pronunciation.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
  </div>
</div>
